{
  "requirement": "An application supporting tracked source inspection returns `Self::NodeData` for the requested path and selector. The SDK interns that data in the domain's cache to obtain `NodeId<Self>`. An unsupported or invalid address returns an error. The cache retains the address when the SDK maps a source item. For source identities the application can supply independently, implement `source_address` to recover the project-relative outline address from the domain identity. Other identities return `None`.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    // ...\n    fn source_node(\n        &self,\n        item: &OutlineData,\n    ) -> Result<Self::NodeData, SourceError> { ... }\n    fn source_address(&self, _data: &Self::NodeData) -> Option<OutlineData> { ... }\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately cover `requirements.sdk.sources.source_nodes`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. `source_node` returns `NodeData` for a path and selector, and the SDK interns it to get a `NodeId`.\n2. An unsupported or invalid address returns an error.\n3. The cache retains the address when the SDK maps a source item.\n4. `source_address` recovers the project-relative outline address for identities the application can supply, and returns `None` for others.\n\n**Coverage**\n- **Mapping and interning.**\n  - `project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[direct_source_reads_preserve_mapping_errors_and_record_only_successful_returns]` calls `read_source` for a supported address.\n  - It asserts that the domain's `source_node` ran (`read_nodes == [\"source-node\",\"source-node\"]`).\n  - It asserts that the resulting dependency is `Dependency::Node(intern_node(\"source-node\"), fingerprint)`. That shows the returned data was interned into a `NodeId`.\n- **Errors.** The same test uses a test `Project` domain whose `source_node` rejects an unknown path and an unknown selector (`line[unknown]`).\n  - Both calls return an error containing \"unsupported source item\".\n  - No dependencies are recorded.\n  - No reads happen.\n- **Address retention.**\n  - `configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[configured_agent_uses_domain_source_tools_in_independent_executions]` uses `TestDomain`. It has no `source_address` override, so addresses cannot be recovered from `TestNode`.\n  - The test lists sources and then reads a node by the listed `NodeId`. This resolves to the `visible/selected.txt` snapshot (\"a source snapshot\"). Only an address retained by the cache can explain that.\n  - It also asserts that the domain's `source_node` was called with the expected `OutlineData`.\n  - It runs the whole flow twice, with a fresh recording each time.\n- **`source_address` round trip.**\n  - `project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[agent_node_addresses_round_trip_and_reject_inconsistent_identities_before_reads]` reads by `data`, by path and location, and by `node` ID, and gets consistent results.\n  - It rejects inconsistent or invalid addresses (absent selector, absent file, mismatched node and data) before any read. The `reads` counter is unchanged afterwards.\n  - `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[habeas_paths_preserve_opaque_segments_and_separate_all_node_kinds]` asserts that `source_address(&source_node(&method)) == Some(method)`. It also asserts `source_address(...) == None` for every non-source node kind (requirement, reference set, selection, definition, source, site review).\n- **Default behavior.** `tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_without_project_sources_leaves_source_tools_disabled]` asserts that the default `source_address` returns `None`. Per the cited domain review in the repository's evidence, `domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors` covers the default `source_node` returning `Invalid`. Neither test is marked for this requirement. The errors-and-round-trip obligations are already covered by the marked tests, so this is at most a marking nicety.\n\nI found no unacknowledged gap or missing scenario. No `{fixme}` acknowledgments apply.",
